<title>USA: Dow Chemical Co Q3 net down, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Dow Chemical Co Q3 net down, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>MIDLAND, Mich. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			$  1.92		  $  2.15</p>
<p> Net			469,000		  571,000</p>
<p> Sales		  4,992,000		4,884,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 244,400		  265,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>	  NINE MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			$  6.02		  $  6.09</p>
<p> Net		    1,491,000		1,656,000</p>
<p> Sales		 15,150,000	     15,606,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 247,700		  272,100</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 nine months net includes reserve of $330 million or $1.24 a share, taken for Dow Corning Co bankruptcy filing. Dow Chemical has a 50 percent ownership in Dow Corning.</p>
<p>1995 nine months net includes income from Marion Merrill Dow pharmaceutical operation of $18 million, and a gain on the sale of Marion Merrill Dow of $169 million. Dow Chemical sold its 197 million shares of Marion Merrill Dow to Hoechst AG in June 1995 for $5.1 billion, or $25.75 a share.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
</text>
